; ===========================================================================
;  background.tiles -- everything the PPU draws behind the sprites
; ===========================================================================
;  Pixels:  .  backdrop (white by day, black by night)
;           o  the ink colour (grey by day, light grey by night)
;           #  black
;           *  the same white as the backdrop -- opaque but invisible, which
;              is what the sprite-0 split hides behind
;
;  Art rows must start in column one.  Everything else here is a comment.
; ===========================================================================

@bank bg

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $00  nothing at all.  Most of the screen is this tile.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@tile BG_BLANK $00
........
........
........
........
........
........
........
........

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $01  the sprite-0 backdrop.  Solid colour 3, which the palette sets to the
;       same colour as the backdrop, so this reads as blank but is opaque --
;       and a sprite laid over it can therefore register a hit.  That hit is
;       what splits the fixed score bar off the scrolling world below it.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@tile BG_SPR0_PAD $01
********
********
********
********
********
********
********
********

